# UI tokens and primitives

Portals have **two modes**. Product docs (`docs/specification/` + ADR) record whether this portal **pins a design-system package**. Do not name a vendor package in these rules.

## Tokens (L0)

- Use design tokens already defined (e.g. `--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, `--accent`, `--surface`, `--muted`) and Tailwind classes wired to them (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, etc.).
- Do **not** introduce new raw hex/HSL for core layout surfaces.
- Do **not** use raw Tailwind palette utilities for component state. Use semantic tokens: `bg-success`, `bg-warning`, `bg-destructive`, `text-accent`, etc.
- **Pinned package:** the package stylesheet is the runtime token SSOT. Do **not** add a competing `:root` / `@theme` token block in `app/globals.css`. New tokens or token changes belong in a **new package tag** (consumer pin bump), not a host fork.
- **No pin:** extend the token system in `app/globals.css` (`:root` + `@theme inline`) with team alignment, then reference the corresponding utility class.

## Primitives (L1)

- Common section pattern: `Card` + `CardHeader` + `CardTitle` + `CardContent`.
- **Pinned package:** import L1 named exports from the package. Do **not** add new low-level primitives under `components/ui`. Do **not** copy package components into the portal “for the ones we need.” Missing export → fail closed (documented L2+ exception or a new package tag) — never a silent local fork.
- **No pin:** prefer **`components/ui`** before adding new low-level primitives.

Avoid `prose` for body text unless `@tailwindcss/typography` is configured to use the same tokens; prefer explicit `text-foreground` + link utilities (`text-accent`, underline) so typography stays on-brand.

Portal **branding** (logos, portal-specific shell): `docs/project-guidance/branding.md`.
